cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "synesthetic-ai: voxel semantic spaces with superimposed color-sets"
authors:
  - alias: Ziggibot0
type: dataset
keywords:
  - representation learning
  - synesthesia-inspired models
  - interpretability
  - self-supervised learning
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ziggibot0/synesthetic-ai"
abstract: >-
  An experiment in structured semantic representation: text mapped to a
  position in a small voxel grid carrying a SET of colors (HSL, never
  mixed), with brightness as salience and multi-color superposition as
  uncertainty. We test whether such baked-in structure induces geometry
  that an equal-sized continuous embedding lacks, measured by
  structure preservation against a reference embedding space.